.TH "KOSH" "5" "October 26, 2026" "kosh" "Koshka Manual"
.SH NAME
kosh \- declarative specification for command\-line flags, shell
settings, settings files, startup scripts, and the KOSHCONF wire format
.PP
Prerequisites \- Familiarity with kosh(1) invocation and startup files.
.PP
Koshka configures execution semantics and interactive line\-editing
through declarative settings files (\f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R]), procedural
startup scripts (\f[CR]rc.kosh\f[R]), the \f[CR]KOSHCONF\f[R]
environment payload, and command\-line flags.
Every shell instance loads settings files before evaluating any startup
script, regardless of whether the session is interactive.
The configured \f[CR]mood\f[R] also governs \f[CR]kosh \-c\f[R]
invocations and scripts that lack a shebang.
.SH CORE CONFIGURATION PRIMITIVES
.PP
